6.System Design and Architecture
Console menu (main.cpp) collects user inputs and calls ContactList operations.
ContactList owns linked-list nodes and manages create/search/update/delete/sort/persistence logic.
Contact encapsulates each record's fields.
Data is persisted in:
data/contacts.txt
The architecture separates the data model, list-management logic, and menu interaction.
7.Class Description
Contact:
Private fields for ID, name, phone, email, city, and notes; getters and setters expose controlled access.
ContactList:
Owns head pointer, next generated ID, and contact count. Its nested Node contains Contact data and a pointer to the next node.
The destructor traverses and deletes all nodes to avoid memory leaks.
8.Data Structures and Algorithms
Singly Linked List:
Dynamic storage with Node .
Linear Search:
Traverses nodes for ID or phone; name search checks a substring.
Insertion Sort:
Temporarily collects node pointers into a vector and shifts Contact values in sorted order. The linked nodes' links are not changed.
File Persistence:
Uses sequential line processing with pipe delimiters and backslash escaping.
